1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,570
Test 2

2
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:03,030
Part 1

3
00:00:03,030 --> 00:00:03,494
Tim:

4
00:00:03,494 --> 00:00:04,058
Good morning.

5
00:00:04,058 --> 00:00:06,800
You're through to the tourist information office,

6
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,090
Tim speaking.How can I help you?

7
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:09,140
Jean:

8
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:10,264
Oh hello.

9
00:00:10,264 --> 00:00:14,570
Could you give me some information about next month's festival, please?

10
00:00:14,570 --> 00:00:19,000
My family and I will be staying in the town that week.

11
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,316
Tim:

12
00:00:19,316 --> 00:00:19,948
Of course.

13
00:00:19,948 --> 00:00:23,740
Well it starts with a concert on the afternoon of the 17th.

14
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:24,076
Jean:

15
00:00:24,076 --> 00:00:25,754
Oh I heard about that.

16
00:00:25,754 --> 00:00:29,110
The orchestra and singers come from the USA, don't they?

17
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:29,614
Tim:

18
00:00:29,614 --> 00:00:31,128
They're from Canada.

19
00:00:31,128 --> 00:00:33,650
They're very popular over there.

20
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:38,356
They're going to perform a number of well-known pieces that will appeal to children

21
00:00:38,356 --> 00:00:39,700
as well as adults.

22
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:40,064
Jean:

23
00:00:40,064 --> 00:00:41,155
That sounds good.

24
00:00:41,155 --> 00:00:43,700
My whole family are interested in music.

25
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:44,171
Tim:

26
00:00:44,171 --> 00:00:50,770
The next day, the 18th, there's a performance by a ballet company called Eustatis.

27
00:00:50,770 --> 00:00:51,255
Jean:

28
00:00:51,255 --> 00:00:51,740
Sorry?

29
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:53,020
Tim:

30
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:59,420
The name is spelt E-U-S-T-A-T-I-S.

31
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:01,542
They appeared in last year's festival,

32
00:01:01,542 --> 00:01:03,310
and went down very well.

33
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:07,060
Again, their programme is designed for all ages.

34
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:07,409
Jean:

35
00:01:07,409 --> 00:01:07,758
Good.

36
00:01:07,758 --> 00:01:09,850
I expect we'll go to that.

37
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:15,270
I hope there's going to be a play during the festival, a comedy, ideally.

38
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:15,610
Tim:

39
00:01:15,610 --> 00:01:16,630
You're in luck!

40
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:21,766
On the 19th and 20th a local amateur group are performing one written by

41
00:01:21,766 --> 00:01:23,600
a member of the group.

42
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:24,906
It's called Jemima.

43
00:01:24,906 --> 00:01:28,390
That will be on in the town hall.

44
00:01:28,390 --> 00:01:31,040
They've already performed it two or three times.

45
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,803
I haven't seen it myself,

46
00:01:32,803 --> 00:01:36,330
but the review in the local paper was very good.

47
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:36,717
Jean:

48
00:01:36,717 --> 00:01:39,040
And is it suitable for children?

49
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:39,445
Tim:

50
00:01:39,445 --> 00:01:43,897
Yes, in fact it's aimed more at children than at adults,

51
00:01:43,897 --> 00:01:46,730
so both performances are in the afternoon.

52
00:01:46,730 --> 00:01:47,204
Jean:

53
00:01:47,204 --> 00:01:49,100
And what about dance?

54
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:51,470
Will there be any performances?

55
00:01:51,470 --> 00:01:51,810
Tim:

56
00:01:51,810 --> 00:01:53,510
Yes, also on the 20th,

57
00:01:53,510 --> 00:01:54,870
but in the evening.

58
00:01:54,870 --> 00:02:00,964
A professional company is putting on a show of modern pieces, with electronic music

59
00:02:00,964 --> 00:02:02,270
by young composers.

60
00:02:02,270 --> 00:02:02,650
Jean:

61
00:02:02,650 --> 00:02:03,030
Uh-huh.

62
00:02:03,030 --> 00:02:03,395
Tim:

63
00:02:03,395 --> 00:02:05,947
The show is about how people communicate,

64
00:02:05,947 --> 00:02:08,500
or fail to communicate, with each other,

65
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:12,250
so it's got the rather strange name, Chat.

66
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:12,636
Jean:

67
00:02:12,636 --> 00:02:18,040
I suppose that's because that's something we do both face to face and online.

68
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:18,990
Tim:

69
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:20,890
That's right.

70
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:21,412
Tim:

71
00:02:21,412 --> 00:02:26,110
Now there are also some workshops and other activities.

72
00:02:26,110 --> 00:02:29,044
They'll all take place at least once every day,

73
00:02:29,044 --> 00:02:32,630
so everyone who wants to take part will have a chance.

74
00:02:32,630 --> 00:02:33,220
Jean:

75
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:33,810
Good.

76
00:02:33,810 --> 00:02:36,760
We're particularly interested in cookery

77
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:40,100
–you don't happen to have a cookery workshop, do you?

78
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:40,453
Tim:

79
00:02:40,453 --> 00:02:41,513
We certainly do.

80
00:02:41,513 --> 00:02:46,460
It's going to focus on how to make food part of a health lifestyle,

81
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:52,457
and it'll show that even sweet things like cakes can contain much less sugar

82
00:02:52,457 --> 00:02:54,170
than they usually do.

83
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:54,537
Jean:

84
00:02:54,537 --> 00:02:56,741
That might be worth going to.

85
00:02:56,741 --> 00:02:59,680
We're trying to encourage our children to cook.

86
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:00,102
Tim:

87
00:03:00,102 --> 00:03:02,631
Another workshop is just for children,

88
00:03:02,631 --> 00:03:07,690
and that's on creating posters to reflect the history of the town.

89
00:03:07,690 --> 00:03:12,676
The aim is to make children aware of how both the town

90
00:03:12,676 --> 00:03:16,000
and people's lives have changed over the centuries.

91
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,540
The results will be exhibited in the community centre.

92
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:23,145
Then the other workshop is in toy-making,

93
00:03:23,145 --> 00:03:25,720
and that's for adults only.

94
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:26,162
Jean:

95
00:03:26,162 --> 00:03:27,490
Oh, why's that?

96
00:03:27,490 --> 00:03:27,959
Tim:

97
00:03:27,959 --> 00:03:33,590
Because it involves carpentry – participants will be making toys out of wood,

98
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:38,110
so there will be a lot of sharp chisels and other tools around.

99
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:38,447
Jean:

100
00:03:38,447 --> 00:03:41,480
It makes sense to keep children away from it.

101
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:41,882
Tim:

102
00:03:41,882 --> 00:03:42,283
Exactly.

103
00:03:42,283 --> 00:03:46,700
Now let me tell you about some of the outdoor activities.

104
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:49,460
There will be supervised wild swimming …

105
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:50,028
Jean:

106
00:03:50,028 --> 00:03:51,164
Wild swimming?

107
00:03:51,164 --> 00:03:52,300
What's that?

108
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:52,688
Tim:

109
00:03:52,688 --> 00:03:57,350
It just means swimming in natural waters, rather than a swimming pool.

110
00:03:57,350 --> 00:03:57,737
Jean:

111
00:03:57,737 --> 00:03:58,512
Oh OK.

112
00:03:58,512 --> 00:04:00,450
In a lake, for instance.

113
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:00,781
Tim:

114
00:04:00,781 --> 00:04:03,761
Yes, there's a beautiful one just outside the town,

115
00:04:03,761 --> 00:04:06,740
and that will be the venue for the swimming.

116
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:09,130
There will be lifeguards on duty,

117
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:11,520
so it's suitable for all ages.

118
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:17,000
And finally, there will be a walk in some nearby woods every day.

119
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,650
The leader is an expert on insects.

120
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:23,175
He'll show some that live in the woods,

121
00:04:23,175 --> 00:04:25,700
and how important they are for the environment.

122
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:30,136
So there are going to be all sorts of different things to do during

123
00:04:30,136 --> 00:04:30,770
the festival.

124
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:31,208
Jean:

125
00:04:31,208 --> 00:04:32,520
There certainly are.

126
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:32,839
Tim:

127
00:04:32,839 --> 00:04:37,300
If you'd like to read about how the preparations for the festival are going,

128
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,530
the festival organizer is keeping a blog.

129
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:42,731
Just search online for the festival website,

130
00:04:42,731 --> 00:04:44,560
and you'll find it.

131
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:44,908
Jean:

132
00:04:44,908 --> 00:04:48,040
Well, thank you very much for all the information.

133
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:48,455
Tim:

134
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:49,285
You're welcome.

135
00:04:49,285 --> 00:04:49,700
Goodbye.

136
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,850
Jean:

137
00:04:50,850 --> 00:04:52,000
Goodbye.
